[ti:Polymorphic Defunctionalization Through Lambda Set Specialization]
[00:04.20]The Roc on the kick has a crack in its beak.
[00:08.72]Three amps hum and the fourth one squeals.
[00:13.20]One good KNOCK from the flat upstairs
[00:15.25]shakes the rust off the ride cymbal.
[00:17.30]Our drummer grins at the ceiling stain.
[00:19.65]“Play me whatever she just played again.”
[00:25.85]Repeat wears a number sewn in its cuff.
[00:30.30]Add-One comes in with its pockets turned out.
[00:34.50]Either can take that knock from my hands.
[00:36.90]I watch your thumb to see which one comes down.
[00:39.10]You give me Repeat with a five tucked inside.
[00:43.30]I hammer five copies out of one.
[00:47.75]You mouth the word twice through a curtain of dust.
[00:52.10]Five fives roll off the tongue of the drum.
[00:55.70]Give us one knock!
[00:59.90]We’ll give it teeth.
[01:03.90]Whoever’s keeping time up there,
[01:06.90]there’s a whole band underneath.
[01:13.60]Keep time, keep time
[01:17.60]till the joists begin to sing.
[01:22.00]We can get the whole house moving
[01:26.50]off the back of one small thing.
[01:31.20]Add-One gets a turn at the head of the stairs.
[01:36.00]One beat grows a second, two grow three.
[01:40.30]Same word twice in your chipped black teeth,
[01:42.45]a different little engine underneath.
[01:44.65]The bulb swings left. The bulb swings right.
[01:48.70]There’s plaster in the beer again tonight.
[01:57.05]POLYMORPHIC!
[01:59.20]DEFUNCTIONALIZATION!
[02:03.95]THROUGH LAMBDA SET SPECIALIZATION!
[02:08.90]Somewhere in the wreckage of that last syllable
[02:12.70]the bass player finds the one.
[02:14.65]Give us one knock!
[02:18.55]We’ll give it teeth.
[02:22.35]One name left on the set this time.
[02:25.40]Wire that name straight to me.
[02:29.00]You slip me a seven. Same hands, same skin.
[02:32.65]Seven strokes, then sevenfold.
[02:34.60]The little brass screws walk out of the kick.
[02:41.65]The crack in the Roc strikes gold.
[02:43.55]Forty-eight hits, and we choke the strings.
[02:45.85]Leave a hole one heartbeat wide.
[02:49.95]For the first time all night we hear her laugh.
[02:52.40]Forty-nine comes from the other side.
